{"id":1105,"path":"/grammar-points/b1/question-tags/","parentId":341,"order":240,"section":"grammar-points","level":"b1","depth":3,"title":"Question tags: Aren’t you? don’t you?","seo":{"title":"Question tags: Aren't you? don't you? - Test-English","description":"Master question tags in English with this B1 Intermediate grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/B1%E2%80%93Tag-questions.png"},"modified":"2026-03-03T08:26:16","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct form to complete the question tags&nbsp;below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"254\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct form for each question tag&nbsp;below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"255\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Fill in the gaps with&nbsp;the correct question tags.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"256\"></div>"],"explanation":"<p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-29879\" src=\"/media/uploads/Question-tags_Grammar-chart.png\" alt=\"Informative grammar chart demonstrating how to form question tags in English, with examples for positive and negative statements across different verb tenses and modal verbs.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h3>Meaning</h3> <p>Question tags are used at the end of statements to turn the statements into questions. We usually use question tags to confirm something that we believe to be true or to invite the listener to agree or disagree with a statement.<br> <br> When we use question tags, the way our voice goes up or down at the end can change the meaning.</p> <div class=\"textBox\"> <strong>Voice goes up ⤴</strong><br> <br> This means we’re not sure about what we’re saying, and we’re really asking for help to know if it’s true or not. For example, “You’re coming to the party, aren’t you?” said with your voice going up is like saying, “Please tell me if you are coming because I don’t know.”<br> <br> <strong>Voice goes down ⤵</strong><br> <br> This means we’re pretty sure about what we’re saying, and we just want the other person to agree with us. For example, “It’s hot today, isn’t it?” said with your voice going down is like saying, “I think it’s hot and I believe you think so too, right?” </div> <h3>Form</h3> <p>Use the same <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/auxiliary-verbs-do-be-and-have/\"><strong>auxiliary verb</strong></a> as in the main sentence. If there is no auxiliary verb, use <strong>do</strong> for present and <strong>did</strong> for past.<br> <br> Use a <strong>comma</strong> before the question tag and a <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/object-pronouns/\"><strong>subject pronoun</strong></a> at the end (<strong>I, you, he, she, it, we, you, they</strong>).</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>You are his brother,<span><strong> aren’t you</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>He will be there, <span><strong>won’t he</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>You work here, <span><strong>don’t you</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>Sam used to live in Scotland, <span><strong>didn’t he</strong></span>?</em></li> </ul> <p>If the main sentence is <strong>positive</strong>, use a <strong>negative</strong> auxiliary.<br> <br> If the main sentence is <strong>negative</strong>, use a <strong>positive</strong> auxiliary.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>You like it, <span><strong>don’t you</strong></span>?</em></li> <li><em>You don’t like it, <span><strong>do you</strong></span>?</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Aren’t I?</strong></h4> <p>❗ <strong>Note</strong> when we have an affirmative sentence with&nbsp;<strong>I am</strong>, the question tag is&nbsp;<strong>aren’t I?</strong></p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’m totally wrong, <span><strong>aren’t I</strong></span>?</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":254,"questions":[{"id":2177,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You are a student, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't you","aren't you","are you"]}]},{"id":2178,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>It isn't too cold today, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["is it","it is","isn't it"]}]},{"id":2179,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He was at the concert, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't he","wasn't it","wasn't he"]}]},{"id":2180,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You like chocolate, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't it","don't you","do you"]}]},{"id":2181,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She arrived too late, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't she","did she","wasn't she"]}]},{"id":2182,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Tom&nbsp;couldn't find the place, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't he","could Tom","could he"]}]},{"id":2183,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Henry and Juliet&nbsp;have just arrived, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["they have","have they","haven't they"]}]},{"id":2184,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Your little Angie can't walk yet, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["she can't","can she","can't she"]}]},{"id":2185,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>When you arrived, she had already left, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["didn't she","she didn't","hadn't she"]}]},{"id":2186,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You would never tell him, <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["would you","would he","wouldn't you"]}]}]},{"id":255,"questions":[{"id":2187,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I'm not interrupting anything, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3115,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>I am</span>"},{"id":3116,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>aren't I</span>"},{"id":3117,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>am I</span>"}]},{"id":2188,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I am quite stupid, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3118,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>aren't I</span>"},{"id":3119,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>am I not</span>"},{"id":3120,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>am I</span>"}]},{"id":2189,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I should go now, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3121,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>aren't I</span>"},{"id":3122,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>shouldn't I</span>"},{"id":3123,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>don't I</span>"}]},{"id":2190,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Elisabeth has passed the test, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3124,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>has she</span>"},{"id":3125,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>hasn't she</span>"},{"id":3126,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>hasn't Elisabeth</span>"}]},{"id":2191,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You won't do anything stupid, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3127,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>will you</span>"},{"id":3128,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>shall you</span>"},{"id":3129,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>won't you</span>"}]},{"id":2192,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>They had already been in Paris, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3130,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>didn't they</span>"},{"id":3131,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>had they</span>"},{"id":3132,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>hadn't they</span>"}]},{"id":2193,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Jimmy&nbsp;passed the exam, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3133,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>doesn't he</span>"},{"id":3134,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>didn't he</span>"},{"id":3135,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>isn't it</span>"}]},{"id":2194,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You work nights, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3136,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>are you</span>"},{"id":3137,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>do you</span>"},{"id":3138,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>don't you</span>"}]},{"id":2195,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>David was trying to hide something from us, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3139,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>wasn't he</span>"},{"id":3140,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>weren't he</span>"},{"id":3141,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>was he</span>"}]},{"id":2196,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Peter&nbsp;can't keep a secret, ______?</div>","choices":[{"id":3142,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>isn't he</span>"},{"id":3143,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>does he</span>"},{"id":3144,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>can he</span>"}]}]},{"id":256,"questions":[{"id":2197,"num":"","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><strong>Dialogue 1</strong><br> <br> A: You&nbsp;haven't washed the dishes, <span class=\"numBox\">1</span> <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?<br> B: No, sorry. I didn't have time. And you are angry now, <span class=\"numBox\">2</span> <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>?<br> A: Well, if you promise&nbsp;you will do something, you should do it, <span class=\"numBox\">3</span> <span data-gap=\"2\"></span>?<br> B:&nbsp;Yes, yes, OK, mum! You want me to wash them now, <span class=\"numBox\">4</span> <span data-gap=\"3\"></span>?<br> A: Of course I want you to wash&nbsp;them now, because you won't pay me to wash them for you, <span class=\"numBox\">5</span> <span data-gap=\"4\"></span>?<br> <br> <strong>Dialogue 2</strong><br> <br> A:&nbsp;&nbsp;You went to Denali National Park last month, <span class=\"numBox\">6</span> <span data-gap=\"5\"></span>?<br> B:&nbsp;Yes, it was great!<br> A:&nbsp;But you had been there before, <span class=\"numBox\">7</span> <span data-gap=\"6\"></span>?<br> B:&nbsp;Yes, but when&nbsp;you really loved a&nbsp;place the first time you went, it's always nice to go back, <span class=\"numBox\">8</span> <span data-gap=\"7\"></span>?<br> A: Of course. I'm sure the views are amazing.<br> B: Yes, they're great. You have never been there, <span class=\"numBox\">9</span> <span data-gap=\"8\"></span>?<br> A: No, it's a shame. I suppose I should go one day, <span class=\"numBox\">10</span> <span data-gap=\"9\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}